  "solution": {
    "text": "<blockquote><p>In steady state, capacitor behaves as open circuit, so no current will flow.</p><p>The total resistance of the circuit is,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>R</mi><mo>=</mo><mfenced><mrow><mn>6</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#937;</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>10</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#937;</mi></math></p><p>The current flowing through the circuit is</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>I</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>10</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#937;</mi></mrow></mfrac></math></p><p>Potential difference on&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>6</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#937;</mi></math>&nbsp;resistor</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>V</mi><mo>&#39;</mo><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>3</mn><mn>10</mn></mfrac><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>6</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>8</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi></math></p><p>The charge on the capacitor is,</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Q</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>C</mi><mi>V</mi><mo>&#39;</mo><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>&#956;F</mi><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>8</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>7</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>&#956;C</mi></math></p></blockquote>",
